{
  "id": "Compound::DB00975 - Gene::10846",
  "verbalization": "Dipyridamole is shown to interact with multiple PDE enzymes, including Pde11a, Pde6a, and Pde7a, through binding interactions. These interactions are linked to the regulation of cyclic nucleotide metabolism, with Pde11a and Pde6a participating in the breakdown of cyclic-GMP and cyclic-nucleotide signaling. The shared involvement of Pde10a in these processes suggests a potential functional overlap, where the inhibition of these PDEs by Dipyridamole may influence the same downstream signaling pathways. The evidence indicates that Dipyridamole may modulate Pde10a through its effects on cyclic nucleotide metabolism, potentially by altering the activity of other PDEs that are part of the same regulatory network. This integrated pathway highlights the role of PDEs in cyclic nucleotide signaling and suggests that Dipyridamole could exert its effects through a mechanism involving the modulation of these enzymes.",
